Declare a model whose shape matches what is actually sent on the wire. FastAPI builds the documented schema from whatever Pydantic model you put under the model key in responses: it takes that model, generates its JSON Schema, and places it under content, application/json, schema (as a $ref into components/schemas). It has no knowledge that HTTPException wraps your payload in detail, so declare that wrapper yourself:

class HttpErrorResponse_PlaylistNotFound(BaseModel):
    detail: HttpError_PlaylistNotFound

@app.get(
    "/playlists/{playlist_id}",
    responses={404: {"model": HttpErrorResponse_PlaylistNotFound,
                     "description": "Playlist not found"}},
)

Your raising code stays exactly as it is; only the declared model changes.

Alternative shown in the docs: instead of model, write the response content into responses directly, giving a content block with application/json and your own schema or example for that status code. FastAPI keeps the extra information from responses and combines it into the OpenAPI output.
